// What the game knows about each clip beyond its keys. GENERATED by tools/clips/build.mjs from the probe's measurements
// (src/chars/clipprobe.js) and the choices in tools/clips/curated.mjs: edit that file and run
//   node --import ./tools/clips/three_node.mjs tools/clips/build.mjs
// Times are seconds into the clip at speed 1. Distances are in the character's own units (a 1.8 m figure: multiply by
// the Cantor's scale for the world). +z is forward, +x is the character's left. See docs/modules/animation.md.
//
//   kind        'move' | 'attack' | 'cast' | 'dodge' | 'jump' | 'turn' | 'react' | 'death' | 'idle' | 'act'
//   loop        plays round and round (default: by name)
//   groundSpeed for walks and runs: metres a second the ground passes under the planted feet; dir: [x, z] its direction
//   travel      [x, z] the whole clip's own travel (handed back by Character.update as root motion)
//   yaw, turn   the clip turns him: the turn (degrees, + = to his left) is taken out and handed back as root motion
//   trim        [t0, t1] the useful stretch of a clip with dead time: play(name, { trim: true }) starts at t0, is done at t1
//   rate        a speed that suits the clip in play (a suggestion: play() does not apply it)
//   speed, fade defaults for play(); speed MULTIPLIES what the caller passes (none is set today)
//   weapon      the attack hits with this bone (a kick, a pommel), not with the blade
//   iframes     [t0, t1] a suggestion for when a dodge cannot be hit
//   recover     when control may come back (after the last hit of an attack; when a roll or a flinch is over)
//   hits        how many cuts an attack has; each has events swing / hit-on / hit-off with data.n = 0, 1, ...
//   events      [{ t, name, data? }]: foot-l, foot-r, swing, hit-on, hit-off, land, and what a clip needs
//   marks       { name: seconds } moments of a clip worth cutting or keying to (the hand reaches the hilt, she is upright)
//   floor       [t, dy, t, dy, ...] how much the hips are raised (+) or lowered (-) over the clip so that the body rests
//               on the floor (measured on the mesh by tools/clips/floor.mjs; applied when c.floorFit is on)
//   stance      walks and runs: [left down, left up, right down, right up] when each foot stands on the ground
//   apart       the clip presses the hands together and on these bodies they pass into each other: move the wrists this
//               far apart (own units; applied with floorFit)
//   headBack    the most the head may lean back from the chest in this clip, degrees (applied softly, with floorFit)
//   kneel       [from, to, side, ...] when the clip kneels and on which knee (0 left, 1 right): with floorFit that knee
//               is brought down to the floor (the clips kneel as a crouch with the knee in the air)
//   $contact    per character: points on the soles, the toes and the hands, in each bone's own frame, that are kept
//               out of the floor; $floorOn, $plantOn: whether Character starts with floorFit and footPlant on
//   $body       per character: the body's shape, measured on the mesh (tools/clips/body.mjs): for each part (a bone) a
//               radial map in the bone's own frame: how far the skin stands from the bone's own line (+y) at nh heights
//               (h0, h0 + dh, ...) and na directions round it; $arm: points on the skin of forearm, hand and fingers,
//               each in its own bone's frame, that are kept out of the body; $bodyOn: whether Character starts with
//               bodyFit on (it acts only while the fighter is a puppet: Character.bodyFit)
//   body        false: the body fit leaves this clip's arms alone
//   $rest       per character: the constant turn per bone that puts the clips' rest pose right (the clip files rest in a
//               T-pose, the model in the pose it was uploaded in); $restOn: whether Character applies it
//   $fix        per character: further constant turns by hand, { Bone: [x, y, z] degrees }

